# The site's calendar, part 1 (design › Backups: "run a quarterly application restore from the
# offsite store ... count the rows against production"; R1.60). A reminder to a person, from
# core so it doesn't depend on infra. The weekly rehearsal on core already restores the
# Vaultwarden dump; this is the fuller, by-hand one (Forgejo and Postgres row counts).
[Unit]
Description=Reminder: the quarterly application restore is due
[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/seed-notify "Quarterly: application restore" 3 "Due: restore the Forgejo and Postgres dumps from B2 (not the local copy) into scratch containers and count rows against production (design, Backups; R1.60). Also refresh BOTH recovery pack copies, A and B (runbooks/recovery-order.md). Record it in the diary."
